{{!-- ONE SEASON'S BLOCK ON A SINGLE-TRACK TIMELINE.

      A marker on the spine carrying the season's glyph and its name, then the cards filed under it.
      The aggregate window does NOT use this partial: a row there is one season across every thread
      and the cards hang off the lanes rather than off the block, so it lays its own row out and
      renders the same cards inside it.

      The heading itself is the shared partial, so this block and the aggregate's row head cannot
      come to name the same season two different ways.

      A YEAR HEADING opens the block wherever the year moves on (`startsYear`), so a long campaign
      reads in years first and seasons within them.

      AN AGE'S BARE YEAR (`ageMark`) is the heading alone: nothing is written in it, and it is
      opened only so an Age's band has its year to lie under.

      A writer's list ends in the season's add slot (`add`); the clock's season with nothing in it
      yet is drawn as a GHOST holding only that slot (timeline-view.js#withGhostNow).

      Context: one period view-model (timeline-view.js#periodVM). --}}
{{#if startsYear}}
<h2 class="stonetop-timeline-year" data-year="{{year}}"{{#if ageMark}} data-age-mark{{/if}}>{{> stonetop.timeline-year-chip}}</h2>
{{/if}}
{{#unless ageMark}}
<section class="stonetop-timeline-period{{#if ghost}} stonetop-timeline-period--ghost{{/if}}" data-period="{{key}}"{{#unless undated}} data-year="{{year}}"{{/unless}}>
	<header class="stonetop-timeline-period-head{{#if seasonClass}} {{seasonClass}}{{/if}}{{#if seasonNotes.length}} stonetop-timeline-head--notes{{/if}}">
		{{~> "stonetop.timeline-period-head"}}
	</header>

	<ol class="stonetop-timeline-cards">
		{{#each entries}}{{> "stonetop.timeline-card"}}{{/each}}
		{{#if add}}{{> "stonetop.timeline-add-slot" add}}{{/if}}
	</ol>
</section>
{{/unless}}
